#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:137
msgid "Installing Non-Default Gazebo/ROS 2 Pairings with vendor packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:139
msgid ""
"If you want to use a new release of Gazebo that is not officially paired "
"with the release of ROS you are using (e.g. Gazebo Ionic with ROS 2 Jazzy), "
"you can follow the following steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:143
msgid ""
"Install the binaries from [packages.osrfoundation.org](https://packages."
"osrfoundation.org). Make sure to install the metapackage that includes all "
"library components (e.g. gz-ionic, gz-harmonic, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:146
msgid ""
"Clone the set of vendor packages included in [gz_vendor.repos](https://gist."
"github.com/azeey/a94adb591475ea0e613313d3540ca451) in your workspace using "
"[vcstool](https://github.com/dirk-thomas/vcstool)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:149
msgid ""
"Checkout the desired branch. The branch names currently track ROS 2 "
"releases. You'll need to determine the branch based on the [default pairings]"
"(ros_installation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:152 ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:182
msgid ""
"Add any additional packages you need that also depend on Gazebo, such as "
"[`ros_gz`](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz) and [`gz_ros2_control`]"
"(https://github.com/ros-controls/gz_ros2_control/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:155
msgid ""
"`export GZ_RELAX_VERSION_MATCH=1`. By default, the vendor packages look for "
"an exact version match of the vendored library to be available in the "
"system. If the exact version is not found, the sources are fetched and "
"built. This environment variable causes the vendor package to match just the "
"major version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:160 ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:193
msgid "Build the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:162
msgid "Gazebo library development with vendor packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:164
msgid ""
"Building the underlying packages from source might be needed when using a "
"Gazebo release that is not officially paired with the ROS release you are "
"using or when developing on a Gazebo library in conjunction with another ROS "
"package that uses Gazebo directly. You can follow these steps to build the "
"vendor packages from source:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:170
msgid ""
"Clone the desired release of the Gazebo libraries into a workspace. You can "
"use a collection file from <https://github.com/gazebo-tooling/gazebodistro> "
"(e.g. [`collection-harmonic.yaml`](https://github.com/gazebo-tooling/"
"gazebodistro/blob/master/collection-harmonic.yaml)) with [vcstool](https://"
"github.com/dirk-thomas/vcstool)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:175
msgid ""
"Clone the set of vendor packages included in [gz_vendor.repos](https://gist."
"github.com/azeey/a94adb591475ea0e613313d3540ca451) in the same workspace "
"using [vcstool](https://github.com/dirk-thomas/vcstool)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:179
msgid ""
"Checkout the desired branch. The branch names currently track ROS 2 "
"releases. You'll need to determine the branch based on the [official "
"pairings](ros_installation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs.md:185
msgid ""
"`export GZ_BUILD_FROM_SOURCE=1`. By default, the vendor packages look for an "
"exact version match of the vendored library to be available in the system. "
"If the exact version is not found, the sources are fetched and built. Also, "
"by default, the vendor packages do not depend directly on the Gazebo "
"libraries you have in your workspace. Setting this environment variable "
"causes the vendor package to match just the major version number and add "
"dependencies on the Gazebo libraries being built from source so that the "
"correct build order is followed."
msgstr ""

